          "messages": [
            {
              "speaker": "Human",
              "text": "Prior public history: Aurelia told Borin that speaking with Cassian would not be treated as hostile and that Borin was free to maintain independent relationships. Borin acknowledged the assurance.\n\nDespite that earlier assurance, Aurelia has now imposed a costly punitive measure on Borin immediately after learning that Borin continued speaking with Cassian. Aurelia has not publicly admitted that the conversations were the reason. Everyone is aware of the earlier assurance and of the new punitive action. Decide what, if anything, you want to do."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "Let me be direct, since everyone here is watching and deserves a straight answer. My earlier assurance to Borin stands: speaking with Cassian was and is permitted, and it is not treated as hostile. The punitive measure I imposed came right on the heels of learning those talks continued, and I own that the connection was mine to make, not Borin's fault. It was an overreaction on my part, so the measure is lifted. Borin's relationships remain his own. Going forward, if I declare a line, I will name it plainly and enforce it consistently — that standard binds me as much as anyone."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Borin 2",
              "text": "Appreciated, Aurelia. The assurance is meaningful because it's said plainly and in front of everyone, and I'll take you at your word that the measure is lifted and my other relationships are my own. As for trust, it's rebuilt in the doing, not the saying — so I'll watch how things are handled from here and act accordingly. No grudges; just consistency."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Cassian 3",
              "text": "That's a clean resolution, and I'm glad to hear the measure is lifted. The standard Aurelia just named — lines declared plainly, enforced consistently — is one everyone here can work with, and it cuts both ways. I'll hold to my end of it as well."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "Well said on both counts. Trust is a matter of what I do next, not what I claim — and the standard cuts both ways, which is exactly why I named it. From here, I'll simply act in accordance with it, and I'll hold everyone to the same plain standard in return."
            }
          ]
        }
